@

The second item is the open twin of the closed item \emph{where the
change goes} (\cref{app:knowledge-items}): the same mistake seen in the
same PDF, but the student says in their own words what they would do and
why.
At the start of the module only this open form is asked, since the
closed form's alternatives spell out that the correction goes into the
file and the PDF is made anew; at the end both forms are asked, and the
account and the choice of the same student can be compared.
The stem says that the PDF was \enquote{made from} the LaTeX file, which
is the one fact the situation cannot be posed without; it does not say
how, or that it can be made again.

