The fourth item shows an error message and asks what it says and what
the student would do next.
The message is a real one---an environment left open when the document
ends---and not one of those the closed items use, so the account is
not primed by a closed item's alternatives later, nor the closed item
by the account.
The stem does not say \enquote{error}: whether the student reads the
text as information, as noise or as a verdict is what the account
should show (\cref{sec:errors}).

