The fifth item is the open twin of \emph{two ways to make a heading}:
two lines of LaTeX that produce the same large bold word in the PDF.
The stem states only that they look the same and asks what, if anything,
differs; an account that finds no difference, one that finds a difference
in looks, and one that finds a difference in what the document
\emph{knows} are three ways of experiencing markup (\cref{sec:markup}).

