The platform shows such a text as the item's feedback; the first line
says what the list is, and the list runs from the least to the most
powerful way of seeing.

<<outcome space: what LaTeX is>>=
"feedback": {"neutral": "<p>Different answers to this question show different ways of seeing LaTeX. In order, from a first impression to the way of seeing the module aims at:</p><ol><li>LaTeX is a program for making good-looking documents&mdash;a word processor with codes in it.</li><li>LaTeX is a notation: you write text with commands in it, and some program turns that into a PDF.</li><li>LaTeX is two things and a step between them: the file <em>is</em> the document, the PDF is made from it each time LaTeX is run, and the commands say what things are while the document class decides how they look.</li></ol>"}
