The compiler reads, it does not watch (\cref{sec:compilation}): the PDF
reflects the last run, and nothing changes until the next one.
The distractors expect the PDF to track the file live, as a word
processor's single window does, or take the mismatch for a fault.
The stem describes the two windows and says nothing about how the PDF
came to be; the key says \enquote{made again}, not \enquote{compiled},
so that the word does not give the alternative away
\autocite[p.~91]{NCOL}.

