Whitespace and characters mean things (\cref{sec:compilation}): the file
is written in a formal language, so repeated spaces collapse and a blank
line starts a paragraph---the layout of the file is not copied to the
page.
The distractors read the file as decorated text whose spacing is
reproduced literally, as the only kind of meaning, or as a fault.
The stem shows the lines and asks what comes out; it does not say that
spaces are \enquote{special}, which is the aspect.

