\subsubsection{Errors and debugging the document}

An error message is information (\cref{sec:errors}): it names a place and
a cause.
The correct choice reads both out of the report; the distractors read the
message as something else, or as meaningless.
The stem shows the message and asks which statement is true; it does not
say that the message is to be read, nor where the line number points.

